1
00:00:00,354 --> 00:00:02,064
(Penny:)What is he doing now?

2
00:00:02,231 --> 00:00:06,151
(Leonard:)Mm, he's either isolating the terms
of his formula...

3
00:00:06,319 --> 00:00:08,319
(Leonard:)...and examining them individually...

4
00:00:08,488 --> 00:00:11,618
(Leonard:)...or looking for the alligator
that swallowed his hand...

5
00:00:11,783 --> 00:00:14,203
(Leonard:)...after Peter Pan cut it off.

6
00:00:15,161 --> 00:00:18,581
(Sheldon:)Captain Hook's hand was eaten
by a crocodile, not an alligator.

7
00:00:19,832 --> 00:00:23,122
(Sheldon:)If you're going to mock me,
at least get your facts straight.

8
00:00:23,294 --> 00:00:25,504
(Leonard:)Aye, aye, captain.

9
00:00:26,798 --> 00:00:28,218
(Sheldon:)I can't see it.

10
00:00:28,382 --> 00:00:29,922
(Sheldon:)It just won't coalesce.

11
00:00:30,093 --> 00:00:31,673
(Leonard:)Maybe you need a fresh start.

12
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:34,550
(Sheldon:)You're right.

13
00:00:41,729 --> 00:00:42,769
[TIRES SCREECHING]

14
00:00:42,939 --> 00:00:44,979
[CAR HORN HONKS]

15
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:50,030
(Sheldon:)Great idea, Leonard. Thank you.

